/* pkpm-vars-closure.mac ---------------------------------------------------------
   Closures of the thermal-velocity-normalized (p=1) PKPM kinetic update with the first Fourier
   harmonic, with the characteristic velocity-space edges. The evolved distributions are the eight
   blocks U = [F, G, M0_perp (x, y, z), N_perp (x, y, z)] on the grid of w = v_par/xi, with the
   per-cell constraints (weakly, for every p=1 test function)

     M0(F) = 1,   M1(F) = 0,   M2(F) + 2 M0(G) = 3,   I_perp int M0_perp dw = 0.

   Stage A produces the partial right-hand sides rhs_A (streaming, known forces and sources; not
   the closure terms). Stage B adds (pkpm-kinetic-vel-vol.mac)

     c_0 U                          normalization (c_0 = div u in the continuum), every block
     -d_w(alpha_0 U)                pressure force, alpha_0 = a_P/xi, every block
     -d_w(c w U) + k c U            heating rate, k = 0, 2, 1, 3 for F, G, M0_perp, N_perp
     a_perp F, a_perp . M0, 2 G a_perp   perpendicular force (M0_perp, G, N_perp sources)

   and the fluxes through the two velocity-domain edges w_lo, w_up: the HLL flux of the full w flux
   alpha U + T(U) (alpha = alpha_0 + (c - K) w - (b.grad xi) w^2, T the coupling by beta, t, R_B1)
   against an empty exterior, with the speeds S_L, S_R = alpha + the bounds of T's spectrum taken
   from the closures of the PREVIOUS stage. The edge flux of every block is then linear in the
   closures:

     Phi_e = K_e + (alpha_0 + c w_e) g_e,   K_e = wf_e (k_e U_e + T_e(U_e)) + wu_e U_e,   g_e = wf_e U_e,

   (k_e = -K w_e - (b.grad xi) w_e^2 the known part of alpha; upper edge: wf = 1, wu = 0 when
   S_L > 0 (outflow); wf = wu = 0 when S_R <= 0; otherwise wf = S_R/(S_R - S_L),
   wu = -S_L S_R/(S_R - S_L); the lower edge mirrored). K_e and g_e are constructed as on the interior
   w faces (pkpm-vel-flux-surf.mac): at the pkpmVelFluxNumPts^cdim w-face nodes, from the raw w-flux
   values of the build (gkyl_pkpm_harm_slots.h) and the node functions of gkyl_pkpm_harm_coeffs.h,
   and projected onto p=1 (5 points per direction: exact where the edge is pure outflow, where
   g_e = U_e). The closures are then solved at the 2^cdim Gauss-Legendre nodes, where these p=1
   projections are evaluated. The interior velocity faces telescope, so with N = [M0, M2, M0G, M1,
   ..., mu] of the state, R = [r0, r2, r0G, r1, ..., rho_M] of rhs_A (mu = int M0_perp dw, rho_M its
   rate) and sgn_e = +1 (lower) / -1 (upper), the four constraint rows are a linear system per node
   for (c_0, alpha_0, c, a_perp):

     M0:  c_0 M0 + alpha_0 eF0 + c eF1 = -r0 - KF0
     M1:  c_0 M1 + alpha_0 (M0 + eF1) + c (M1 + eF2) = -r1 - KF1
     E :  c_0 s2 + alpha_0 (2 M1 + eF2 + 2 eG0) + c (2 s2 + eF3 + 2 eG1) + 2 mu . a_perp
          = -(r2 + 2 r0G) - KF2 - 2 KG0,   s2 = M2 + 2 M0G
     perp: M0 a_perp + (c_0 + c) Q + alpha_0 A_a + c A_c = -P

   with eX_k = sum_e sgn_e w_e^k g_X,e, KX_k = sum_e sgn_e w_e^k K_X,e, Q = I_perp mu,
   A_a = I_perp sum_e sgn_e g_M0,e, A_c = I_perp sum_e sgn_e w_e g_M0,e and
   P = I_perp (rho_M + sum_e sgn_e K_M0,e) (b is a unit vector at the closure nodes). The
   perpendicular rows are eliminated into the energy row (Schur complement: the energy row gains
   -(2/M0) Q.(P + (c_0 + c) Q + alpha_0 A_a + c A_c)), the 3x3 is solved by Cramer's rule at the
   2^cdim Gauss-Legendre nodes, a_perp follows, and everything is interpolated to p=1. The edge
   fluxes of all eight blocks are formed at the same nodes from the SAME closures and written in the
   stored face format of the velocity-flux kernels (shape coefficients: orthonormal surface
   coefficients divided by sqrt(1/2)^cdim (2 sqrt 3/5)^(linear factors of the mode)): the stored edge
   flux is P1(K_e) + P1((alpha_0 + c w_e) P1(g_e)) (the 2-point rule is exact for the product of two
   p=1 fields against a p=1 test function), so that what the velocity pass applies at the edges is
   exactly what the closure charged. On the constraint manifold (mu = 0) the system is block
   diagonal; where the distribution does not reach the edges all edge terms vanish.

   Policy: if M0(F) <= 0 or the determinant is not positive at any node, all closures and the edge
   fluxes are zero in the cell and the kernel returns the number of such nodes.

   Time step (plan 17.27): every velocity-space rate is a polynomial in w of degree <= 2, so with
   absolute coefficients evaluated at W = max(|w_lo|, |w_up|) it bounds every w of the column.
   cfl[0] receives that column rate of the w fluxes and the closure sources:
   (2 p_v + 1)/2 dv1 max over the w-face nodes of |alpha_0| + |c - K| W + |b.grad xi| W^2 + (the
   coupling's spectrum bound at W), plus max over the cell of |c_0| + 3 |c| (the source eigenvalues
   c_0 + k c, k = 0..3; the a_perp couplings are nilpotent), bounded by the absolute modal
   coefficients times the largest value of each mode. With the new closures; zero closures where
   they are undefined. cfl[1] = 0. */

load("core/modal-basis.mac")$
load("util_maxima/out-scripts.mac")$
load("core/nodal_operations/quadrature_functions.mac")$
load("pkpm/pkpm/pkpm-flux-tables.mac")$
load("pkpm/pkpm/pkpm-cas-util.mac")$
load("pkpm/pkpm/pkpm-nodal.mac")$
load(stringproc)$
fpprec : 24$

cvarsClo : [x, y, z]$

calcPKPMVarsClosure(fh, funcNm, cdim, basisFun, polyOrder) := block(
  [lb, pkC, pkbC, vv, pkbV, pkP, pkbP, NC, NP, nodes, weights, NN, nodeSub, n, k, d, i, c, nlin,
   n0_e, n1_e, n2_e, nG_e, r0_e, r1_e, r2_e, rG_e, mu_e, rM_e, b_e, h_e, pidx, sOf, xw, x1, w1, NQ, NF,
   p1fn, c0_c, a0_c, c_c, sc, lst, mmax],

  lb : loadPKPMPhaseBasis(cdim),
  pkC : copylist(lb[1]), pkbC : copylist(lb[2]), vv : lb[3][1], pkbV : copylist(lb[4]),
  pkP : copylist(lb[5]), pkbP : copylist(lb[6]),
  NC : length(pkbC),
  NP : length(pkbP),
  /* the closure nodes */
  [nodes, weights] : gaussOrdWeight(2, cdim),
  NN : length(nodes),
  nlin : makelist(length(listofvars(pkbC[k])), k, 1, NC),
  /* the w-face nodes, direction 0 fastest (those of the build and of the interior w faces) */
  pidx : pkpmPhaseIndex(pkC, pkbC, vv, pkbV, pkbP),
  sOf : pkpmP1PatternIndex(pkC, pkbC),
  xw : gaussOrdWeight1D(pkpmVelFluxNumPts), x1 : float(xw[1]), w1 : float(xw[2]),
  NQ : length(x1), NF : NQ^cdim,
  p1fn : sconcat(funcNm, "_p1"),
  /* the largest value over the cell of each orthonormal p=1 mode */
  mmax : makelist(float((1/sqrt(2))^(cdim - nlin[k])*sqrt(3/2)^nlin[k]), k, 1, NC),

  printf(fh, "#include <gkyl_pkpm_vars_kernels.h> ~%"),
  printf(fh, "#include <gkyl_pkpm_harm_coeffs.h> ~%~%"),
  pkpmEmitP1Nodes(fh, p1fn, cdim, sOf, x1),
  printf(fh, "// Projection of node values onto the p=1 basis (orthonormal coefficients, gkyl order). ~%"),
  pkpmEmitNodeProj(fh, sconcat(funcNm, "_prj"), cdim, NQ,
    [makelist(w1[i]/sqrt(2), i, 1, NQ), makelist(w1[i]*sqrt(3/2)*x1[i], i, 1, NQ)], sOf),
  printf(fh, "GKYL_CU_DH int ~a(double w_lo, double w_up, double dv, const double *norm_moms, const double *rhs_moms,
  const double *bvar, const double *wn, const double *theta, const double *alpha_0_prev, const double *c_h_prev,
  const double *f_lo, const double *f_up,
  double* GKYL_RESTRICT c_0, double* GKYL_RESTRICT alpha_0, double* GKYL_RESTRICT c_h, double* GKYL_RESTRICT a_perp,
  double* GKYL_RESTRICT flux_lo, double* GKYL_RESTRICT flux_up, double* GKYL_RESTRICT cfl,
  double* GKYL_RESTRICT cond) ~%{ ~%", funcNm),
  printf(fh, "  // w_lo, w_up:   Velocity domain edges; dv: velocity cell size. ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  // norm_moms:    Input [M0, M2, M0_G, M1, M3, M1_G, mu (x, y, z)] moments of the normalized distributions (stage state). ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  // rhs_moms:     Input moments of the stage-A right-hand sides, same layout. ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  // bvar:         Magnetic field unit vector [bx, by, bz]. ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  // wn:           Raw w-flux values at the ~a w-face nodes [node][PKPM_HS_W_END] (the build of the stored operator). ~%", NF),
  printf(fh, "  // theta:        T_perp/T. ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  // alpha_0_prev, c_h_prev: closures of the previous stage (may alias the outputs), for the edge speeds. ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  // f_lo, f_up:   [F, G, M0_perp, N_perp] of the lowest and uppermost velocity cells of this configuration cell. ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  // c_0, alpha_0, c_h, a_perp: Output closures at the ~a Gauss-Legendre nodes, interpolated to p=1. ~%", NN),
  printf(fh, "  // flux_lo, flux_up: Output edge fluxes [8 blocks] in the stored face format. ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  // cfl:          Output [0]: the time-step rate of the w fluxes and closure sources of the whole column ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  //               (absolute coefficients at the larger |w| edge, plan 17.27); [1] = 0. ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  // cond:         Output [1]: the smallest determinant of the 3x3 system over the nodes relative to ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  //               its edge-free value (1 when the edge terms vanish; small or negative when the ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  //               velocity-domain edges carry a non-negligible trace: too small velocity extents). ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  // Returns the number of nodes where the closures are undefined (everything is zero in the cell then). ~%"),
  printf(fh, " ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  const double dv1 = 2.0/dv; ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  const double *n0 = &norm_moms[~a]; ~%", 0*NC),
  printf(fh, "  const double *n2 = &norm_moms[~a]; ~%", 1*NC),
  printf(fh, "  const double *nG = &norm_moms[~a]; ~%", 2*NC),
  printf(fh, "  const double *n1 = &norm_moms[~a]; ~%", 3*NC),
  printf(fh, "  const double *r0 = &rhs_moms[~a]; ~%", 0*NC),
  printf(fh, "  const double *r2 = &rhs_moms[~a]; ~%", 1*NC),
  printf(fh, "  const double *rG = &rhs_moms[~a]; ~%", 2*NC),
  printf(fh, "  const double *r1 = &rhs_moms[~a]; ~%", 3*NC),
  for i : 1 thru 3 do printf(fh, "  const double *mu~a = &norm_moms[~a]; ~%", i-1, (5+i)*NC),
  for i : 1 thru 3 do printf(fh, "  const double *rM~a = &rhs_moms[~a]; ~%", i-1, (5+i)*NC),
  for i : 1 thru 3 do printf(fh, "  const double *b~a = &bvar[~a]; ~%", i-1, (i-1)*NC),
  printf(fh, " ~%"),

  /* 1. the edge fluxes at the w-face nodes, as on the interior w faces, split into the known part
     K and the part g multiplying alpha_0 + c w_e; both projected onto p=1 */
  printf(fh, "  // The edge fluxes at the ~a w-face nodes, constructed as on the interior w faces (traces, raw ~%", NF),
  printf(fh, "  // node values, HLL against the empty exterior with the previous closures): ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  // Phi_e = K_e + (alpha_0 + c w_e) g_e, K_e = wf (k_e U + T(U)) + wu U, g_e = wf U, e = lower, upper. ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  double tr[~a], ulo[8][~a], uup[8][~a]; ~%", NC, NF, NF),
  for c : 0 thru 7 do (
    pkpmEmitTrace(fh, "tr", f_lo, c, -1, NP, pidx, pkbV, vv),
    printf(fh, "  ~a(tr, ulo[~a]); ~%", p1fn, c),
    pkpmEmitTrace(fh, "tr", f_up, c, 1, NP, pidx, pkbV, vv),
    printf(fh, "  ~a(tr, uup[~a]); ~%", p1fn, c)
  ),
  pkpmEmitWNodeFields(fh, p1fn, NF, NC, "alpha_0_prev", "c_h_prev"),
  printf(fh, "  double Kn[2][8][~a], gn[2][8][~a], kw[~a], rest[~a]; ~%", NF, NF, NF, NF),
  printf(fh, "  const double wm = fmax(fabs(w_lo), fabs(w_up)); ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  for (int n = 0; n < ~a; ++n) { ~%", NF),
  printf(fh, "    double nv[PKPM_HS_NODE_NV]; ~%"),
  pkpmEmitWNodeFill(fh, "    ", "nv"),
  printf(fh, "    kw[n] = nv[PKPM_HS_KW]; ~%"),
  printf(fh, "    rest[n] = pkpm_harm_node_speed_rest(nv, wm); ~%"),
  printf(fh, "    for (int e = 0; e < 2; ++e) { ~%"),
  printf(fh, "      const double w = e == 0 ? w_lo : w_up; ~%"),
  printf(fh, "      double U[8], T[8], lo, hi; ~%"),
  printf(fh, "      for (int c = 0; c < 8; ++c) U[c] = e == 0 ? ulo[c][n] : uup[c][n]; ~%"),
  printf(fh, "      pkpm_harm_node_coupling(nv, w, U, T); ~%"),
  printf(fh, "      pkpm_harm_node_bounds(nv, w, &lo, &hi); ~%"),
  printf(fh, "      const double k = pkpm_harm_node_alpha_k(nv, w); ~%"),
  printf(fh, "      const double ap = nv[PKPM_HS_NODE_A0] + nv[PKPM_HS_NODE_CH]*w + k; ~%"),
  printf(fh, "      const double sl = ap + lo, sr = ap + hi; ~%"),
  printf(fh, "      // the HLL flux against the empty exterior (below the lower edge, above the upper one): ~%"),
  printf(fh, "      // wf (alpha U + T(U)) + wu U ~%"),
  printf(fh, "      double wf = 0.0, wu = 0.0; ~%"),
  printf(fh, "      if (e == 0) { ~%"),
  printf(fh, "        if (sr < 0.0) { ~%"),
  printf(fh, "          wf = 1.0; ~%"),
  printf(fh, "        } else if (sl < 0.0) { ~%"),
  printf(fh, "          wf = -sl/(sr - sl); wu = sl*sr/(sr - sl); ~%"),
  printf(fh, "        } ~%"),
  printf(fh, "      } else { ~%"),
  printf(fh, "        if (sl > 0.0) { ~%"),
  printf(fh, "          wf = 1.0; ~%"),
  printf(fh, "        } else if (sr > 0.0) { ~%"),
  printf(fh, "          wf = sr/(sr - sl); wu = -sl*sr/(sr - sl); ~%"),
  printf(fh, "        } ~%"),
  printf(fh, "      } ~%"),
  printf(fh, "      for (int c = 0; c < 8; ++c) { ~%"),
  printf(fh, "        Kn[e][c][n] = wf*(k*U[c] + T[c]) + wu*U[c]; ~%"),
  printf(fh, "        gn[e][c][n] = wf*U[c]; ~%"),
  printf(fh, "      } ~%"),
  printf(fh, "    } ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  } ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  double Kh[2][~a], gh[2][~a]; ~%", 8*NC, 8*NC),
  printf(fh, "  for (int e = 0; e < 2; ++e) { ~%"),
  printf(fh, "    for (int c = 0; c < 8; ++c) { ~%"),
  printf(fh, "      ~a_prj(Kn[e][c], &Kh[e][c*~a]); ~%", funcNm, NC),
  printf(fh, "      ~a_prj(gn[e][c], &gh[e][c*~a]); ~%", funcNm, NC),
  printf(fh, "    } ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  } ~%"),
  printf(fh, " ~%"),

  /* 2. the closures at the 2^cdim Gauss-Legendre nodes */
  n0_e : doExpand1(n0, pkbC), n1_e : doExpand1(n1, pkbC), n2_e : doExpand1(n2, pkbC), nG_e : doExpand1(nG, pkbC),
  r0_e : doExpand1(r0, pkbC), r1_e : doExpand1(r1, pkbC), r2_e : doExpand1(r2, pkbC), rG_e : doExpand1(rG, pkbC),
  mu_e : makelist(doExpand1(concat(mu, i-1), pkbC), i, 1, 3),
  rM_e : makelist(doExpand1(concat(rM, i-1), pkbC), i, 1, 3),
  b_e : makelist(doExpand1(concat(b, i-1), pkbC), i, 1, 3),
  h_e : doExpand1(h, pkbC),

  printf(fh, "  // The closures at the ~a Gauss-Legendre nodes, with the edge fluxes' p=1 projections there. ~%", NN),
  printf(fh, "  double c0_s[~a] = {0.0}, a0_s[~a] = {0.0}, c_s[~a] = {0.0}; ~%", NN, NN, NN),
  printf(fh, "  double ap_s[3][~a] = {{0.0}}, flo_s[8][~a] = {{0.0}}, fup_s[8][~a] = {{0.0}}; ~%", NN, NN, NN),
  printf(fh, "  int num_null = 0; ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  double cond_min = 1.0; ~%"),
  printf(fh, " ~%"),
  for n : 1 thru NN do (
    nodeSub : makelist(pkC[d]=nodes[n][d], d, 1, cdim),
    printf(fh, "  { ~%"),
    printf(fh, "    const double n0_q = ~a; ~%", float(expand(subst(nodeSub, n0_e)))),
    printf(fh, "    const double n1_q = ~a; ~%", float(expand(subst(nodeSub, n1_e)))),
    printf(fh, "    const double n2_q = ~a; ~%", float(expand(subst(nodeSub, n2_e)))),
    printf(fh, "    const double nG_q = ~a; ~%", float(expand(subst(nodeSub, nG_e)))),
    printf(fh, "    const double r0_q = ~a; ~%", float(expand(subst(nodeSub, r0_e)))),
    printf(fh, "    const double r1_q = ~a; ~%", float(expand(subst(nodeSub, r1_e)))),
    printf(fh, "    const double r2_q = ~a + 2.0*(~a); ~%", float(expand(subst(nodeSub, r2_e))), float(expand(subst(nodeSub, rG_e)))),
    printf(fh, "    const double mu_q[3] = {~a, ~a, ~a}; ~%", float(expand(subst(nodeSub, mu_e[1]))), float(expand(subst(nodeSub, mu_e[2]))), float(expand(subst(nodeSub, mu_e[3])))),
    printf(fh, "    const double rM_q[3] = {~a, ~a, ~a}; ~%", float(expand(subst(nodeSub, rM_e[1]))), float(expand(subst(nodeSub, rM_e[2]))), float(expand(subst(nodeSub, rM_e[3])))),
    printf(fh, "    const double b_q[3] = {~a, ~a, ~a}; ~%", float(expand(subst(nodeSub, b_e[1]))), float(expand(subst(nodeSub, b_e[2]))), float(expand(subst(nodeSub, b_e[3])))),
    printf(fh, "    // the p=1 projections of the edge fluxes' parts at the node ~%"),
    printf(fh, "    double Klo[8], Kup[8], glo[8], gup[8]; ~%"),
    printf(fh, "    for (int c = 0; c < 8; ++c) { ~%"),
    printf(fh, "      const double *h = &Kh[0][c*~a]; ~%", NC),
    printf(fh, "      Klo[c] = ~a; ~%", float(expand(subst(nodeSub, h_e)))),
    printf(fh, "      h = &Kh[1][c*~a]; ~%", NC),
    printf(fh, "      Kup[c] = ~a; ~%", float(expand(subst(nodeSub, h_e)))),
    printf(fh, "      h = &gh[0][c*~a]; ~%", NC),
    printf(fh, "      glo[c] = ~a; ~%", float(expand(subst(nodeSub, h_e)))),
    printf(fh, "      h = &gh[1][c*~a]; ~%", NC),
    printf(fh, "      gup[c] = ~a; ~%", float(expand(subst(nodeSub, h_e)))),
    printf(fh, "    } ~%"),
    printf(fh, "    // edge contributions to the moment rates: the k-th moment gains sgn_e w_e^k Phi_e per edge, ~%"),
    printf(fh, "    // sgn_e = +1 lo, -1 up: closure part (alpha_0 + c w_e) g_e and known part K_e ~%"),
    printf(fh, "    const double eF0 = glo[0] - gup[0]; ~%"),
    printf(fh, "    const double eF1 = w_lo*glo[0] - w_up*gup[0]; ~%"),
    printf(fh, "    const double eF2 = w_lo*w_lo*glo[0] - w_up*w_up*gup[0]; ~%"),
    printf(fh, "    const double eF3 = w_lo*w_lo*w_lo*glo[0] - w_up*w_up*w_up*gup[0]; ~%"),
    printf(fh, "    const double eG0 = glo[1] - gup[1]; ~%"),
    printf(fh, "    const double eG1 = w_lo*glo[1] - w_up*gup[1]; ~%"),
    printf(fh, "    const double KF0 = Klo[0] - Kup[0]; ~%"),
    printf(fh, "    const double KF1 = w_lo*Klo[0] - w_up*Kup[0]; ~%"),
    printf(fh, "    const double KF2 = w_lo*w_lo*Klo[0] - w_up*w_up*Kup[0]; ~%"),
    printf(fh, "    const double KG0 = Klo[1] - Kup[1]; ~%"),
    printf(fh, "    // perpendicular rows M0 a_perp + (c_0 + c) Q + alpha_0 A_a + c A_c = -P (b is a unit vector here) ~%"),
    printf(fh, "    double P[3], Q[3], Aa[3], Ac[3], v[3]; ~%"),
    printf(fh, "    for (int a = 0; a < 3; ++a) v[a] = rM_q[a] + Klo[2 + a] - Kup[2 + a]; ~%"),
    printf(fh, "    pkpm_harm_perp(b_q, v, P); ~%"),
    printf(fh, "    pkpm_harm_perp(b_q, mu_q, Q); ~%"),
    printf(fh, "    for (int a = 0; a < 3; ++a) v[a] = glo[2 + a] - gup[2 + a]; ~%"),
    printf(fh, "    pkpm_harm_perp(b_q, v, Aa); ~%"),
    printf(fh, "    for (int a = 0; a < 3; ++a) v[a] = w_lo*glo[2 + a] - w_up*gup[2 + a]; ~%"),
    printf(fh, "    pkpm_harm_perp(b_q, v, Ac); ~%"),
    printf(fh, "    // eliminated into the energy row, which carries 2 mu . a_perp (Schur complement) ~%"),
    printf(fh, "    const double fac = n0_q > 0.0 ? 2.0/n0_q : 0.0; ~%"),
    printf(fh, "    const double sQQ = pkpm_harm_dot(Q, Q), sQP = pkpm_harm_dot(Q, P), sQA = pkpm_harm_dot(Q, Aa), sQC = pkpm_harm_dot(Q, Ac); ~%"),
    printf(fh, "    // 3x3 system A [c_0, alpha_0, c] = rhs: stage-A rates + interior stage-B rates + edge rates = 0 ~%"),
    printf(fh, "    const double A00 = n0_q, A01 = eF0, A02 = eF1; ~%"),
    printf(fh, "    const double A10 = n1_q, A11 = n0_q + eF1, A12 = n1_q + eF2; ~%"),
    printf(fh, "    const double A20 = n2_q + 2.0*nG_q - fac*sQQ, A21 = 2.0*n1_q + eF2 + 2.0*eG0 - fac*sQA, A22 = 2.0*(n2_q + 2.0*nG_q) + eF3 + 2.0*eG1 - fac*(sQQ + sQC); ~%"),
    printf(fh, "    const double b0 = -r0_q - KF0, b1 = -r1_q - KF1, b2 = -r2_q - KF2 - 2.0*KG0 + fac*sQP; ~%"),
    printf(fh, "    const double det = A00*(A11*A22 - A12*A21) - A01*(A10*A22 - A12*A20) + A02*(A10*A21 - A11*A20); ~%"),
    printf(fh, "    // conditioning proxy: the determinant relative to its edge-free value ~%"),
    printf(fh, "    // n0 (2 n0 (M2 + 2 M0G) - 2 M1^2) (positive for admissible moments); a small or negative ~%"),
    printf(fh, "    // ratio means the traces at the velocity-domain edges are not small ~%"),
    printf(fh, "    const double det0 = n0_q*(2.0*n0_q*(n2_q + 2.0*nG_q) - 2.0*n1_q*n1_q); ~%"),
    printf(fh, "    if (det0 > 0.0) cond_min = fmin(cond_min, det/det0); ~%"),
    printf(fh, "    if (n0_q > 0.0 && det > 0.0) { ~%"),
    printf(fh, "      c0_s[~a] = (b0*(A11*A22 - A12*A21) - A01*(b1*A22 - A12*b2) + A02*(b1*A21 - A11*b2))/det; ~%", n-1),
    printf(fh, "      a0_s[~a] = (A00*(b1*A22 - A12*b2) - b0*(A10*A22 - A12*A20) + A02*(A10*b2 - b1*A20))/det; ~%", n-1),
    printf(fh, "      c_s[~a] = (A00*(A11*b2 - b1*A21) - A01*(A10*b2 - b1*A20) + b0*(A10*A21 - A11*A20))/det; ~%", n-1),
    printf(fh, "      for (int a = 0; a < 3; ++a) ~%"),
    printf(fh, "        ap_s[a][~a] = -(P[a] + (c0_s[~a] + c_s[~a])*Q[a] + Aa[a]*a0_s[~a] + Ac[a]*c_s[~a])/n0_q; ~%", n-1, n-1, n-1, n-1, n-1),
    printf(fh, "      for (int c = 0; c < 8; ++c) { ~%"),
    printf(fh, "        flo_s[c][~a] = (a0_s[~a] + c_s[~a]*w_lo)*glo[c] + Klo[c]; ~%", n-1, n-1, n-1),
    printf(fh, "        fup_s[c][~a] = (a0_s[~a] + c_s[~a]*w_up)*gup[c] + Kup[c]; ~%", n-1, n-1, n-1),
    printf(fh, "      } ~%"),
    printf(fh, "    } else { ~%"),
    printf(fh, "      num_null += 1; ~%"),
    printf(fh, "    } ~%"),
    printf(fh, "  } ~%")
  ),
  printf(fh, " ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  cond[0] = cond_min; ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  if (num_null > 0) { ~%"),
  printf(fh, "    // a node with M0 <= 0 or a non-positive determinant zeroes everything in the cell (the ~%"),
  printf(fh, "    // closures it would have needed are not applied); the rate is that of the known w fluxes ~%"),
  printf(fh, "    double rate = 0.0; ~%"),
  printf(fh, "    for (int n = 0; n < ~a; ++n) { ~%", NF),
  printf(fh, "      rate = fmax(rate, fabs(kw[n])*wm + rest[n]); ~%"),
  printf(fh, "    } ~%"),
  printf(fh, "    cfl[0] = 2.5*dv1*rate; cfl[1] = 0.0; ~%"),
  printf(fh, "    for (int k = 0; k < ~a; ++k) { ~%", NC),
  printf(fh, "      c_0[k] = 0.0; alpha_0[k] = 0.0; c_h[k] = 0.0; ~%"),
  printf(fh, "    } ~%"),
  printf(fh, "    for (int k = 0; k < ~a; ++k) { ~%", 3*NC),
  printf(fh, "      a_perp[k] = 0.0; ~%"),
  printf(fh, "    } ~%"),
  printf(fh, "    for (int k = 0; k < ~a; ++k) { ~%", 8*NC),
  printf(fh, "      flux_lo[k] = 0.0; flux_up[k] = 0.0; ~%"),
  printf(fh, "    } ~%"),
  printf(fh, "    return num_null; ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  } ~%"),
  printf(fh, " ~%"),

  /* nodal -> modal (2-point rule, exact for p=1) for the closures; the edge fluxes in the
     stored face format (orthonormal coefficient / shape factor). */
  c0_c : makelist(sum(weights[n]*subst(makelist(pkC[d]=nodes[n][d], d, 1, cdim), pkbC[k])*c0_s[n-1], n, 1, NN), k, 1, NC),
  a0_c : makelist(sum(weights[n]*subst(makelist(pkC[d]=nodes[n][d], d, 1, cdim), pkbC[k])*a0_s[n-1], n, 1, NN), k, 1, NC),
  c_c : makelist(sum(weights[n]*subst(makelist(pkC[d]=nodes[n][d], d, 1, cdim), pkbC[k])*c_s[n-1], n, 1, NN), k, 1, NC),
  writeCExprs1(c_0, c0_c),
  writeCExprs1(alpha_0, a0_c),
  writeCExprs1(c_h, c_c),
  printf(fh, " ~%"),
  /* The nodal-to-modal maps of a_perp and of the fluxes as loops over the components. */
  printf(fh, "  for (int a = 0; a < 3; ++a) { ~%"),
  for k : 1 thru NC do (
    printf(fh, "    a_perp[a*~a + ~a] = ", NC, k-1),
    lst : makelist(float(weights[n]*subst(makelist(pkC[d]=nodes[n][d], d, 1, cdim), pkbC[k])), n, 1, NN),
    for n : 1 thru NN do printf(fh, "~a(~a)*ap_s[a][~a]", if n > 1 then " + " else "", lst[n], n-1),
    printf(fh, "; ~%")
  ),
  printf(fh, "  } ~%"),
  sc : makelist(sqrt(2)^cdim*(5/(2*sqrt(3)))^nlin[k], k, 1, NC),
  printf(fh, "  for (int c = 0; c < 8; ++c) { ~%"),
  for k : 1 thru NC do (
    lst : makelist(float(sc[k]*weights[n]*subst(makelist(pkC[d]=nodes[n][d], d, 1, cdim), pkbC[k])), n, 1, NN),
    printf(fh, "    flux_lo[c*~a + ~a] = ", NC, k-1),
    for n : 1 thru NN do printf(fh, "~a(~a)*flo_s[c][~a]", if n > 1 then " + " else "", lst[n], n-1),
    printf(fh, "; ~%"),
    printf(fh, "    flux_up[c*~a + ~a] = ", NC, k-1),
    for n : 1 thru NN do printf(fh, "~a(~a)*fup_s[c][~a]", if n > 1 then " + " else "", lst[n], n-1),
    printf(fh, "; ~%")
  ),
  printf(fh, "  } ~%"),
  printf(fh, " ~%"),
  /* 3. the column time-step rate with the new closures: the w-flux speed bound at the w-face nodes
     and the closure sources over the cell */
  printf(fh, "  // the column time-step rate with the new closures (plan 17.27) ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  double a0f[~a], cf[~a]; ~%", NF, NF),
  printf(fh, "  ~a(alpha_0, a0f); ~%", p1fn),
  printf(fh, "  ~a(c_h, cf); ~%", p1fn),
  printf(fh, "  double rate = 0.0; ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  for (int n = 0; n < ~a; ++n) { ~%", NF),
  printf(fh, "    rate = fmax(rate, fabs(a0f[n]) + fabs(cf[n] + kw[n])*wm + rest[n]); ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  } ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  double src = 0.0; ~%"),
  for k : 1 thru NC do
    printf(fh, "  src += ~a*(fabs(c_0[~a]) + 3.0*fabs(c_h[~a])); ~%", mmax[k], k-1, k-1),
  printf(fh, "  cfl[0] = 2.5*dv1*rate + src; ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  cfl[1] = 0.0; ~%"),
  printf(fh, " ~%"),
  printf(fh, "  return 0; ~%"),
  printf(fh, "} ~%")
)$
